submission.root_cause:
In ccp_run_sha_cmd, the context size check only validates sha->ctx_len against the digest size (e.g. 20 bytes for SHA-1, 48 for SHA-384), but the non-final "Stash the context" path and the restore path always move sb_count * CCP_SB_BYTES (32 or 64) bytes to/from sha->ctx. A caller-supplied context buffer smaller than the full SB slot can therefore be written past its end (or read past its end on restore). I did not confirm the exact upstream fix, so this patch is a best-effort guess at the intended bound check.</root_cause>
